          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em free diagram
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is a particularly simple special case of the general concept of a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ℐ
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet \;\colon\; \mathcal{I} \to \mathcal{C}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℐ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{I}
            of the diagram is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+category"} free category
          %p
            Many important types of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            are over free diagrams, for instance
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizers"} equalizers
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizers"} coequalizers
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushouts"} pushouts
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+limits"} sequential limits
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+colimits"} sequential colimits
          %p
            Due to the simplicity of the concept of free diagrams, these types of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            may be discussed in a very low-brow way, without even making the concept of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            and
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            explicit. For this see the
            %em
              %a{:href => "#Exposition"} Exposition
            below.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p Recall that
          #Diagram.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"}> diagram
                )
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℐ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{I}
                  , the
                  %em shape
                  of the diagram;
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
