          #FreeCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+category"}> free category
                )
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free-forgetful+adjunction"} free-forgetful adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi Underlying
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi Free
                    %mi DirGraph
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Cat
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{Underlying}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{Free}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    DirGraph
            %p
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-categories"} 1-categories
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
              and that of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+graphs"} directed graphs
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+category"} free category
              is one in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
              of this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Free
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi DirGraph
                    %mo →
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Free \colon DirGraph \to Cat
              (sometimes called a “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+category"}> path category
              ”).
          #FreeDiagram.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              %strong (free diagram)
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+diagram"} free diagram
              in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Diagram"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+category"} free category
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FreeCategory"}
            %p
              In other words, a free diagram in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+graph"} directed graph
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi I
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                  of the form
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mo •
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi Free
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi I
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo →
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet \;\colon\; Free(I) \to \mathcal{C}
          %h2#examples Examples
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              Types of free diagrams that are commonly encountered in practice, as well as the names of the
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              over them are shown in the following table
            %div
              %p
                %strong
                  shapes of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+diagrams"} free diagrams
                  and the names of their
                  = succeed "/" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              %table
                %thead
                  %tr
                    %th
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+diagram"} free diagram
                    %th
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"}> limit
                      \/
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
                %tbody
                  %tr
                    %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+diagram"} empty diagram
                    %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"}> terminal object
                      \/
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
                  %tr
                    %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+category"} discrete diagram
                    %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"}> product
                      \/
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
                  %tr
                    %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+morphisms"} parallel morphisms
                    %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizer"}> equalizer
                      \/
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
                  %tr
                    %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"}> span
                      \/
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cospan"} cospan
                    %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"}> pullback
                      ,
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+product"}> fiber product
                      \/
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
                  %tr
                    %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tower"}> tower
                      \/
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotower"} cotower
                    %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+limit"}> sequential limit
                      \/
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+colimit"} sequential colimit
          %h2#Exposition Exposition
          %p
            We give an exposition of free diagrams, and their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cones"} cones
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits+and+colimits+by+example"} limits and colimits by example
          %p
            For concreteness, we speak only of diagrams of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            and of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            in the following:
          #Diagram.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+diagram"} free diagram
                of
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+diagram"} free diagram
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
              or of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ X_i \}_{i \in I}
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
                  or of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              %li
                %p
                  for every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                        %mo ×
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i,j) \in I \times I
                  of labels, a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mi α
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi j
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi α
                            %mo ∈
                            %msub
                              %mi I
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo ,
                                %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ X_i \overset{ f_\alpha }{\longrightarrow} X_j\}_{\alpha \in I_{i,j}}
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
                  of of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
          #DiscreteDiagram.num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+category"} discrete
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
                and
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+diagram"} empty diagram
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              be any
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                    %mo ×
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i,j) \in I \times I
              let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                    %mo =
                    %mi ∅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_{i,j} = \emptyset
              be the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty set
            %p
              The corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+diagrams"} free diagrams
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Diagram"}
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+category"} discrete
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            %p
              For example for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I = \{1,2,3\}
              the set with 3-elements, then such a diagram looks like this:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAA
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAA
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 3
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_1 \phantom{AAA} X_2 \phantom{AAA} X_3
                    \\,.
            %p
              Notice that here the index set may be
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                      %mo =
                      %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I = \emptyset
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+diagram"} empty diagram
          #ParallelMorphisms.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+morphisms"} parallel morphisms
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I = \{a, b\}
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              with two elements, and consider the sets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                              %mn 1
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi i
                              %mo =
                              %mi a
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mtext and
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi j
                              %mo =
                              %mi b
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi ∅
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mtext otherwise
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    I_{i,j}
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    \\{ 1,2 \} &amp; \vert &amp; (i = a) \,\text{and}\, (j = b)
                    \\\
                    \\emptyset &amp; \vert &amp; \text{otherwise}
                    }
                    \\right\}
                    \\,.
            %p
              The corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+diagrams"} free diagrams
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Diagram"}
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs+of+parallel+morphisms"} pairs of parallel morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi a
                    %munderover
                      %mphantom
                        %mi AAAAA
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mn 2
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi b
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_a
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{f_2}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{f_1}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\phantom{AAAAA}}
                    X_b
                    \\,.
          #SpanDiagram.num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cospan"} cospan
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I = \{a,b,c\}
              the set with three elements, and set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                              %msub
                                %mi f
                                %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi i
                              %mo =
                              %mi c
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mtext and
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi j
                              %mo =
                              %mi a
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                              %msub
                                %mi f
                                %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi i
                              %mo =
                              %mi c
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mtext and
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi j
                              %mo =
                              %mi b
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi ∅
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mtext otherwise
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    I_{i ,j}
                    \=
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    \\{f_1\} &amp; \vert \, (i = c) \,\text{and}\, (j = a)
                    \\\
                    \\{f_2\} &amp; \vert \, (i = c) \,\text{and}\, (j = b)
                    \\\
                    \\emptyset &amp; \vert \, \text{otherwise}
                    }
                    \\right.
            %p
              The corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+diagrams"} free diagrams
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Diagram"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi c
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi f
                                    %mn 1
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi f
                                    %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi a
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi b
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; X_c
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{f_1}}\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{f_2}}
                    \\\
                    X_a &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; X_b
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              These are called
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagrams"} diagrams
            %p
              Similary, there is the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cospan"} cospan
              diagram of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi c
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
